  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @brief Processing function for Q31 normalized LMS filter.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[in] *S points to an instance of the Q31 normalized LMS filter structure.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[in] *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[in] *pRef points to the block of reference data.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[out] *pOut points to the block of output data.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[out] *pErr points to the block of error data.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @param[in] blockSize number of samples to process.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * @return none.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * \par
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * The accumulator has a 2.62 format and maintains full precision of the intermediate
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * multiplication results but provides only a single guard bit.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * Thus, if the accumulator result overflows it wraps around rather than clip.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * log2(numTaps) bits. The reference signal should not be scaled down.
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * After all multiply-accumulates are performed, the 2.62 accumulator is shifted
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * and saturated to 1.31 format to yield the final result.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * The output signal and error signal are in 1.31 format.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * \par
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * 	In this filter, filter coefficients are updated for each sample and the
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** * updation of filter cofficients are saturted.
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** *
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** */
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** 
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_norm_q31.c **** void arm_lms_norm_q31(
